Subject: [PATCH] The capacity restart, encoded rather than done by hand at six
 in the morning

The principal authorised two changes that both need a restart of the box that trades, and the
window for it is narrow and after a commit freeze. This is the runbook: preconditions, ORDER,
and verification, with the guards tested.

THE ORDER IS THE POINT. MetaTrader READS common.ini at startup and REWRITES it at shutdown, so a
MaxBars edit made while the terminal is up is discarded the next time it closes. The terminal is
stopped FIRST (and the gateway resident before it, or it would restart the terminal), the file is
edited SECOND, the box restarts THIRD. common.ini is UTF-16LE with a BOM and is rewritten as
UTF-16LE -- writing UTF-8 makes the terminal ignore the whole file. `set_maxbars` refuses outright
if the MaxBars key is absent rather than guessing the layout, and keeps a timestamped backup.

MaxBars 100,000 -> 2,000,000, with the arithmetic stated because "never Unlimited" needs a
reason. MqlRates is 60 bytes a bar. 100,000 M1 bars is ~91 trading days, which is what the desk
has today on 248 of 248 symbols (measured 101,169-104,465 per frame, never once a venue end)
while the terminal holds 22.46 GB of .hcc back to 2020 for 108 symbols. 2,000,000 is ~992 trading
days, 10.9x, and reaches that 2020-onward history. Ceiling if every chart that CAN reach the cap
were hot at full depth: M1 248 x 2,000,000 x 60 B = 29.8 GB, M5 ~6.1 GB (7 years is ~508,000
bars, under the cap), M15 ~1.2 GB -- about 37 GB, inside 96 GB of RAM beside the judge's
15-worker pool. The depth lane's "1,736 hot charts at 1M bars is ~100 GB" over-counts twice: only
M1 has the history to reach a seven-figure cap, and 1,736 charts are never hot together.
Unlimited is refused on purpose -- it would let one symbol's M1 take unbounded commit and put the
judge back at the ceiling this restart exists to clear.

PagingFiles -> "C:\pagefile.sys 262144 393216", CommitLimit 245.95 GB -> ~480 GB against 911 GB
free. CommitPeak has equalled CommitLimit exactly, and that ceiling is 129 of 168 recorded pass
deaths (77%): BrokenProcessPool, `handle is closed`, MemoryError, and `DLL load failed ... the
paging file is too small`, all of them a spawning worker failing to allocate.

THE PRECONDITIONS REFUSE, and the tests are mostly about them. It will not stage before
gold_asia (04:00Z) and the family lane (05:00Z) have had their chance and the freeze has ended --
the desk has not placed since 05:56Z and taking its window to save a reboot is the wrong trade.
It reads E8 POSITIONS, never the guard, because "stood down" is not "flat". It refuses if
allows_new_risk is False, so the box is never restarted into a halt nobody has cleared. An
unreadable artifact refuses rather than passing. It will not edit common.ini while the terminal
is still up, and it will not restart unless staging actually succeeded.

Dry run at 01:06Z: REFUSED on windows_had_their_chance and allows_new_risk; e8_flat and mt5_flat
both ok; MaxBars reads 100000.

